PipelineERP consists out of 4 main functions. They are named with capital characters to mark their status. They are saved in pipeline folder, and will be be rarely edited.
Other functions, named with small characters, are consider as subscripts and are saved in in SC_FUNCTIONS folder.

1. sc_1_PREPROC - preprocesses data 

    Consists of: 
    % REREFERENCING
    % REJECTION OF REF. CHANNELS
    % FILTERING OF HIGH AND LOW FREQUENCES
    % REJECTION OF EOG ARTIFACTS
    % REJECTION OF EOG CHANNELS
    % POSSIBLY SAVING CONTINOUS (PREPROCESSED) DATA - to be specified in saveFolder

2. sc_2_SEGM - segments data into epoch

    % This function segments continous data into epoch. 
    % Triggers of interst should be specified in 'EX_SETUP.m' script in 'design' section.
    % It supports both no-recodding and recodding of triggers.
        % If recodding of triggers is needed 'sc_recodding_TEMPLATE.m' script should be edited 
        % and saved in experiment folder with an original name. 
        % It's name is passed along as the 'segm_fun_to_call' parameter to this function. 
        % for more info chek 'sc_recodding_TEMPLATE.m'
    % Parameters such as prestim, poststim and baseline should be specified in EX_SETUP, accordingly to experimental disgign.

3. sc_3_ARTIFACTS - rejects artifacts, accordingly to give specification

    % This function provides code for artifact rejection.

    % 1st stage reject trials which are exceptionally bad.
    % 2nd stage either interpolated exceptionally bad channels or removes entire ds (if more than 8 channels are exceptionally bad)
    % 3rd stage rejects muscle artifacts
    % 4th stage takes care about range artifacts within each trial. If less than 4 channels exceeds threshold it interpolates those channels. If more than than 4 channels exceeds threshold, it removes entire trial.

    For more info look up the function itself or pay attention to given parameters in EX_SETUP_TEMPLATE

4. sc_4_ERPanalysis - This scirpt provides an oportunity to calculate Event Related Potentials 
    from data which has been previously preprocessed, segmented and cleaned up from artifacts. 

5. _sc_VISUALISATION - provides tools to visualise data at different stages of data analysis.

6. _sc_recodding_TEMPLATE - The script provides code which recodes triggers assigned during experiment. It should be edited and saved in experiment folder!

7. _EX_SETUP_TEMPLATE - provides a template of experiment SET_UP. 
!!! Each of exp. parameter should be specified in this script. 
!!! Script itself should be saved in experiment folder!

8. _biosemi64_neighb.mat - provides coordinates of electrodes and 'elec' structure needed for channel interpolation
 


